{
  "id": "randai_minangkabau",
  "name": "Randai (Minangkabau circle theatre)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Minangkabau folk theatre of West Sumatra, documented in detail by Kirstin Pauka, in which a troupe moving in a circle (galombang) alternates silek martial-arts movement with acted scenes and sung episodes (dendang) that tell a kaba story. Between scenes the circle players slap their stretched trousers in interlocking patterns (tapuak galembong; the hand-clap card stands in), and the songs and interludes are accompanied by talempong kettle gongs (the canang card stands in), the saluang end-blown bamboo flute (the generic bamboo-flute card stands in), the sarunai shawm and the gandang drum (the Malay gendang card stands in).",
  "recipe": "classic modern randai, ballad Poetry. canang kettle gong, bamboo credited bamboo flute unspecified, serunai shawm, snappy hand muted gendang melayu, hand clap. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
